BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Wolf of Wall Street (2013)
DTSTART:20260416T023000Z
DTEND:20260416T053000Z
DTSTAMP:20260416T023000Z
UID:5tw3PHk5fa
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 165 mins (2h45m)\n\nMartin Scorsese: Maestro of Cine
 ma In Leonardo DiCaprio’s pet project he’s a Wall Street player who\, 
 with his partner (Jonah Hill)\, scams millions from vulnerable investors. 
 It’s a euphoric ride through the most depraved aspects of our human natu
 re. With the late\, great\, much-loved Rob Reiner.\n\nhttps://www.siff.ne
 t/programs-and-events/martin-scorsese/the-wolf-of-wall-street\n\nEstimated
  start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:STEFF: Birds & Us
DTSTART:20260418T200000Z
DTEND:20260418T215000Z
DTSTAMP:20260418T200000Z
UID:Iyg3TTvxvY
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 91 mins (1h31m)\n\nPresented by GreenShower Collect
 ive Celebrate the historic launch of the 1st Seattle Taiwanese Eco Film F
 estival (STEFF)\, hosted by GreenShower. For the first time\, we are bring
 ing a curated selection of award-winning Taiwanese environmental cinema to
  the United States. This double-feature event explores our delicate bond w
 ith nature: from the investigative journey of Birds and Us to the poignant
  cultural struggle on Orchid Island in Island of People (Pongso no Tao). T
 hese films unveil the hidden environmental and social challenges facing Ta
 iwan’s ecosystems and Indigenous traditions. Join us for this landmark c
 ultural exchange\, featuring an exclusive live remote Q&A session.\n\nhttp
 s://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/1st-seattle-taiwanese-eco-film-festiva
 l-birds-and-us\n\nEstimated start: 13:15
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:STEFF: Island of People (Pongso no Tao)
DTSTART:20260418T223000Z
DTEND:20260419T001500Z
DTSTAMP:20260418T223000Z
UID:RyoUwWFvrv
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 89 mins (1h29m)\n\nPresented by GreenShower Collect
 ive Celebrate the historic launch of the 1st Seattle Taiwanese Eco Film F
 estival (STEFF)\, hosted by GreenShower. For the first time\, we are bring
 ing a curated selection of award-winning Taiwanese environmental cinema to
  the United States. This double-feature event explores our delicate bond w
 ith nature: from the investigative journey of Birds and Us to the poignant
  cultural struggle on Orchid Island in Island of People (Pongso no Tao). T
 hese films unveil the hidden environmental and social challenges facing Ta
 iwan’s ecosystems and Indigenous traditions. Join us for this landmark c
 ultural exchange\, featuring an exclusive live remote Q&A session.\n\nhttp
 s://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/1st-seattle-taiwanese-eco-film-festiva
 l-pongso-no-taoisland-of-people\n\nEstimated start: 15:45
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Silence (2016)
DTSTART:20260423T023000Z
DTEND:20260423T053000Z
DTSTAMP:20260423T023000Z
UID:HZNAKflpsp
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 161 mins (2h41m)\n\nMartin Scorsese: Maestro of Cine
 ma Scorsese chose to show this spiritual thriller\, in which 17th-century 
 priests (Andrew Garfield\, Adam Driver) seek their missing mentor (Liam Ne
 eson) in Japan\, where Christianity is outlawed\, but a visionary voice st
 ill speaks. A meditation on Christian and Buddhist thought\, an illuminati
 on of physical and metaphysical faith. Scorsese as landscape painter.\n\nh
 ttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/martin-scorsese/silence\n\nEstimat
 ed start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Meet Me in St. Louis (1944)
DTSTART:20260426T180000Z
DTEND:20260426T202000Z
DTSTAMP:20260426T180000Z
UID:kZbEf0IxSn
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 123 mins (2h03m)\n\nCommunity ScreeningsIn turn of t
 he century St. Louis\, Judy Garland sings about trollies and pines for “
 Boy Next Door” Tom Drake\, Margaret O’Brien braves the terrors of Hall
 oween\, Mom Mary Astor looks lovely in Technicolored middle-age\, and Dad 
 Leon Ames debates taking that Gotham job as the 1903 World’s Fair beckon
 s.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/community-screenings/meet-m
 e-in-st-louis\n\nEstimated start: 11:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Irishman (2019)
DTSTART:20260430T023000Z
DTEND:20260430T061500Z
DTSTAMP:20260430T023000Z
UID:M007WxsbY1
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 209 mins (3h29m)\n\nMartin Scorsese: Maestro of Cine
 ma A stunning epic panorama of mid-century America\, seen through the yout
 h-to-old age viewpoint of Mob hitman Frank Sheeran (Robert De Niro)\, righ
 t hand man to top Teamster Jimmy Hoffa (Al Pacino). Mafia bosses (Joe Pesc
 i\, Harvey Keitel)\, Kennedy\, Nixon\, Watergate\, are evoked\, but the in
 timate drama center’s on Sheeran's family\, and the consequences of the 
 way he's spent his time.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/marti
 n-scorsese/the-irishman\n\nEstimated start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sansho the Bailiff (1954)
DTSTART:20260505T013000Z
DTEND:20260505T035500Z
DTSTAMP:20260505T013000Z
UID:Fyht286mNG
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 126 mins (2h06m)\n\nSIFF Movie Club One of cinema's 
 greatest masterpieces\, Japanese master Kenji Mizoguchi's empathetic exami
 nation of human resilience in the face of evil takes place in medieval Jap
 an\, where the family of an exiled nobleman are left to fend for themselve
 s and become wrenched apart by vicious slave traders.\n\nhttps://www.siff.
 net/programs-and-events/siff-movie-club/sansho-the-bailiff\n\nEstimated st
 art: 18:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Velvet Goldmine (1998)
DTSTART:20260602T013000Z
DTEND:20260602T031500Z
DTSTAMP:20260602T013000Z
UID:BYmIDtKVIl
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nSIFF Movie Club It’s been 10 ye
 ars since glam-rock superstar Brian Slade (Jonathan Rhys Myers) faked his 
 own death and vanished from the spotlight. Now\, it’s the job of investi
 gative reporter Arthur Stuart (Christian Bale) to locate this living legen
 d and uncover the truth behind his disappearance.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/
 programs-and-events/siff-movie-club/velvet-goldmine\n\nEstimated start: 18
 :45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
